WEBVTT

1
00:01:38.246 --> 00:01:49.072
<font color="#ec14bd">Transcript & sync by honeybunny</font>
<font color="#ec14bd">www.addic7ed.com</font>

2
00:03:11.753 --> 00:03:14.007
Is that Estermont?

3
00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:16.535
Tarth. Ser Jaime.

4
00:03:18.399 --> 00:03:20.257
The Sapphire Isle.

5
00:03:24.582 --> 00:03:26.440
Why are we on a merchant ship?

6
00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.785
Why no Lannister sails?

7
00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:33.164
This ship's sailing to Oldtown.

8
00:03:33.284 --> 00:03:35.417
We'll get off earlier.
not far from Sunspear.

9
00:03:35.537 --> 00:03:38.280
Row ourselves to the Dornish shores
in the night.

10
00:03:39.742 --> 00:03:41.143
You ever been to Dorne?

11
00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:43.091
- No.
- I have.

12
00:03:43.432 --> 00:03:46.746
The Dornish are crazy. All they want to do
is fight and fuck.

13
00:03:46.866 --> 00:03:49.328
- fuck and fight.
- You should be happy to go back.

14
00:03:51.609 --> 00:03:54.508
There's nothing like a good fight
to get you in the mood for fucking.

15
00:03:55.093 --> 00:03:57.334
And there's nothing like
a fuck-mad Dornish girl

16
00:03:57.454 --> 00:03:59.795
to clear your head for the next fight.

17
00:03:59.915 --> 00:04:01.692
It's how the two work together.

18
00:04:01.812 --> 00:04:04.153
And we're gonna do a lot
of fighting. I am sure.

19
00:04:04.273 --> 00:04:08.538
Well. I am. But I don't imagine we'll
get to stick around for the rest.

20
00:04:08.658 --> 00:04:10.609
Not after we've kidnapped their princess.

21
00:04:10.729 --> 00:04:12.841
We are not kidnapping their princess.

22
00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.536
We are rescuing my niece.
bringing her back to the family.

23
00:04:16.091 --> 00:04:17.577
Your niece?

24
00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.502
I've been doing this sort
of thing a long time.

25
00:04:27.622 --> 00:04:28.769
I'm good at it.

26
00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:30.572
- That's why you're here.
- I know.

27
00:04:30.692 --> 00:04:34.564
Why are you here? Why not
send 40 of me. or an army?

28
00:04:34.684 --> 00:04:36.614
Unlike most folks. you actually got one.

29
00:04:37.052 --> 00:04:39.221
Because I don't want to start a war.

30
00:04:40.557 --> 00:04:43.164
That still doesn't explain
why you're doing it.

31
00:04:45.747 --> 00:04:47.330
It has to be me.

32
00:04:50.486 --> 00:04:52.581
If I'm putting something of a lit together.

33
00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.095
a one-handed man.

34
00:04:54.215 --> 00:04:57.846
who happens to be one of the most
recognizable faces in Westeros is not...

35
00:04:57.966 --> 00:04:59.988
It has to be me.

36
00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.148
You set your brother free. didn't you?

37
00:05:08.849 --> 00:05:11.134
I bet your sister didn't like that.

38
00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.245
Varys set him free.

39
00:05:18.202 --> 00:05:20.333
Well...

40
00:05:21.948 --> 00:05:26.211
if you ever see the little fucker.
give him my regards.

41
00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:32.546
He murdered my father.

42
00:05:34.283 --> 00:05:37.816
If I ever see him.
I'll split him in two.

43
00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.105
And then I'll give him your regards.

44
00:05:47.288 --> 00:05:51.369
The Iron Bank has called one
tenth of the Crown's debts.

45
00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:55.967
- Given the expensive rebuilding of...
- How much can the Crown afford?

46
00:05:56.394 --> 00:05:59.470
With winter coming. half what they ask.

47
00:06:00.143 --> 00:06:02.641
- Less.
- You're the Master of Coin.

48
00:06:03.158 --> 00:06:06.904
- How do we pay them?
- House Tyrell could front the gold and the...

49
00:06:07.024 --> 00:06:11.229
the Crown will pay us back in time.
or I'll have words with my daughter.

50
00:06:16.681 --> 00:06:19.543
You've already given us too much.

51
00:06:20.244 --> 00:06:23.107
No. we must arrange better
terms with the Iron Bank.

52
00:06:23.472 --> 00:06:25.482
- Absolutely.
- In person.

53
00:06:27.403 --> 00:06:28.377
Me?

54
00:06:28.497 --> 00:06:30.722
We must send an envoy to the Iron Bank.

55
00:06:30.842 --> 00:06:34.165
someone of importance. to show
these bankers our respect.

56
00:06:34.285 --> 00:06:37.180
As the King's Master of Coin. I can
think of no one more qualified.

57
00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.312
I will be honored. Your Grace.

58
00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:43.393
The King has expressed concern about his
father-in-law's safety on this voyage.

59
00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.852
He's ordered Ser Meryn to
personally lead your escort.

60
00:06:52.623 --> 00:06:54.477
A valiant Kingsguard?

61
00:06:54.597 --> 00:06:56.913
- Please express...
- Safe travels. Lord Tyrell.

62
00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:03.065
Of course. of course. I'll give your
regards to the Titan of Braavos.

63
00:07:11.659 --> 00:07:14.751
The Small Council grows
smaller and smaller.

64
00:07:14.871 --> 00:07:16.268
Not small enough.

65
00:07:27.205 --> 00:07:29.515
May I offer you some wine. Your Holiness?

66
00:07:29.635 --> 00:07:32.037
No.

67
00:07:35.869 --> 00:07:38.058
The old High Septon would
have asked the vintage.

68
00:07:38.178 --> 00:07:41.468
I could say that our minds
are temples to the Seven

69
00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:43.456
and should be kept pure.

70
00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.717
But the truth is.

71
00:07:45.837 --> 00:07:48.250
I don't like the taste.

72
00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.883
How may I serve?

73
00:07:53.168 --> 00:07:56.186
All over Westeros we hear
about septs being burned.

74
00:07:56.793 --> 00:07:58.727
Silent sisters raped.

75
00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:02.369
Bodies of holy men piled in the streets.

76
00:08:02.489 --> 00:08:04.901
Wars teach people to obey the sword.

77
00:08:05.021 --> 00:08:06.148
not the Gods.

78
00:08:06.268 --> 00:08:08.490
Perhaps the Gods need a sword of their own.

79
00:08:09.426 --> 00:08:11.298
In the days before the Targaryens.

80
00:08:11.418 --> 00:08:14.385
the Faith Militant dispensed
the justice of the Seven.

81
00:08:14.505 --> 00:08:18.534
Well. the Faith Militant was disarmed
more than two centuries ago.

82
00:08:19.226 --> 00:08:22.407
If I explain the holy purpose
to my son. the king.

83
00:08:22.983 --> 00:08:27.125
I have no doubt he will sign a decree
arming the believers you find worthy.

84
00:08:27.649 --> 00:08:31.332
An army that defends the bodies
and souls of the common people.

85
00:08:31.452 --> 00:08:34.353
An army and service to the Gods themselves.

86
00:08:34.711 --> 00:08:36.357
And to you. of course.

87
00:08:36.906 --> 00:08:38.752
As the chosen representative of the Seven.

88
00:08:38.872 --> 00:08:41.247
An honor I've never expected.

89
00:08:41.693 --> 00:08:43.502
Or indeed. ever wished for.

90
00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:44.986
Which is why you were chosen.

91
00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:49.571
You and I both know how the world works.

92
00:08:49.845 --> 00:08:53.625
Too often the wicked or the wealthiest
be on the reach of justice.

93
00:08:53.893 --> 00:08:57.336
The king himself cannot always punish those
who deserve it most.

94
00:08:57.772 --> 00:09:00.267
All sinners are equal before the Gods.

95
00:09:04.963 --> 00:09:09.150
What would you say if I told you
we have a great sinner in our own midst?

96
00:09:09.524 --> 00:09:12.237
Shielded by gold and privilege.

97
00:09:14.358 --> 00:09:16.385
May the Father judge him justly.

98
00:09:55.781 --> 00:09:57.527
Help me! Help me!

99
00:10:07.195 --> 00:10:08.180
Aah!

100
00:10:28.388 --> 00:10:30.668
This is Lord Petyr Baelish's establishment.

101
00:10:41.699 --> 00:10:42.946
Cocksucker!

102
00:10:44.622 --> 00:10:46.162
Boy fucker!

103
00:10:46.864 --> 00:10:48.988
You barbaric filth!

104
00:10:49.708 --> 00:10:53.333
There's a special place in the Seven Hells
for your kind.

105
00:10:53.453 --> 00:10:56.159
Please. please. I'll pay!

106
00:10:56.471 --> 00:10:58.576
I'll pay all of you.

107
00:10:58.696 --> 00:11:01.012
Yes. you will!

108
00:11:35.638 --> 00:11:37.041
Seize him.

109
00:11:39.112 --> 00:11:40.487
Get your hands off of me.

110
00:11:40.607 --> 00:11:44.141
Ser Loras of House Tyrell. you have broken
the laws of Gods and men.

111
00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.928
Who do you think you are?

112
00:11:47.746 --> 00:11:49.968
Justice.

113
00:11:55.967 --> 00:11:57.721
Why is my brother in a cell?

114
00:11:58.443 --> 00:11:59.768
I...I don't know.

115
00:12:01.004 --> 00:12:02.349
I...I didn't order it.

116
00:12:02.758 --> 00:12:04.103
We both know who did.

117
00:12:05.155 --> 00:12:08.079
You told me she was
returning to Casterly Rock.

118
00:12:09.619 --> 00:12:11.220
Are you saying my mother is behind this?

119
00:12:11.239 --> 00:12:13.887
She's jealous you're not hers anymore.

120
00:12:14.007 --> 00:12:16.733
Arresting my brother is her revenge.

121
00:12:16.853 --> 00:12:19.016
Aren't you and mother getting along?

122
00:12:24.766 --> 00:12:28.430
Oh. my sweet. sweet King.

123
00:12:30.165 --> 00:12:33.303
Do you have any affection for me at all?

124
00:12:34.736 --> 00:12:36.646
Of course I do.

125
00:12:37.212 --> 00:12:38.654
You're my Queen.

126
00:12:38.774 --> 00:12:43.585
I can't bear to think of my brother locked
away in some grimy cell.

127
00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.678
I'll set him free for you.

128
00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.276
You promise?

129
00:12:56.966 --> 00:12:59.597
I demand that Ser Loras be freed now!

130
00:12:59.929 --> 00:13:01.157
Did I arrest him?

131
00:13:02.657 --> 00:13:04.197
Well. no...

132
00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:07.358
But you armed the Faith Militant.

133
00:13:07.607 --> 00:13:10.211
You gave the High Sparrow an army.

134
00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:11.396
I did.

135
00:13:13.166 --> 00:13:16.236
And your wife has every right to criticize.

136
00:13:17.381 --> 00:13:22.195
Can't allow fanatics to arrest the Queen's
brother. no matter his perversions.

137
00:13:23.053 --> 00:13:24.710
Then...

138
00:13:26.539 --> 00:13:28.675
can I tell Margaery you'll
have Ser Loras released?

139
00:13:28.795 --> 00:13:31.081
I told you I am not holding Ser Loras.

140
00:13:32.102 --> 00:13:36.822
You're the King. I'm sure if you speak to the
High Sparrow. he'll release the poor boy.

141
00:13:42.522 --> 00:13:43.933
Halt!

142
00:14:06.978 --> 00:14:10.689
His Holiness is praying.
He will not be disturbed.

143
00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:15.781
Give the order and we'll
tear out this rebel.

144
00:14:16.709 --> 00:14:20.973
You mean. kill them?
Here. in the sept?

145
00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.676
You'll be sending them to
meet the Gods that they love.

146
00:14:27.825 --> 00:14:29.881
Bastard!

147
00:14:30.718 --> 00:14:33.726
You're an abomination!

148
00:14:36.895 --> 00:14:39.084
You're born of sin!

149
00:14:39.204 --> 00:14:42.034
Filthy bastard!

150
00:14:46.126 --> 00:14:48.553
We'll find another way.

151
00:14:50.567 --> 00:14:52.318
Abomination!

152
00:14:58.085 --> 00:14:59.323
My Queen.

153
00:15:05.066 --> 00:15:07.746
There was no way to free Ser Loras
without violence.

154
00:15:10.894 --> 00:15:12.843
You're the King of the Andals.

155
00:15:13.361 --> 00:15:16.772
the Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.
the Protector of the Realm.

156
00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.731
And you let a band of fanatics
imprison your brother by law.

157
00:15:22.102 --> 00:15:25.086
- I'm going to speak to the High Sparrow.
- Are you? When?

158
00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:29.228
- I...I don't know.
- You don't know?

159
00:15:29.348 --> 00:15:32.335
He was praying just now.

160
00:15:35.061 --> 00:15:37.649
I have to send word to Grandmother.

161
00:15:37.769 --> 00:15:39.781
Will you come back later?

162
00:15:42.332 --> 00:15:44.311
I need to be wit my family. Your Grace.

163
00:15:46.177 --> 00:15:47.297
Of course.

164
00:15:50.434 --> 00:15:52.018
You think highly of this boy.

165
00:15:52.962 --> 00:15:53.875
Good.

166
00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:58.352
- Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.
- A bastard by some tavern slut.

167
00:15:58.472 --> 00:16:01.467
Perhaps. but that wasn't Ned Stark's way.

168
00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.217
I should have given you a son.

169
00:16:09.556 --> 00:16:11.858
- Not your fault.
- Whose then?

170
00:16:13.214 --> 00:16:15.280
I gave you nothing but weakness.

171
00:16:18.535 --> 00:16:19.841
And deformity.

172
00:16:20.893 --> 00:16:23.817
Those scars mean nothing
to the Lord of Light.

173
00:16:23.937 --> 00:16:25.220
My Lady.

174
00:16:26.117 --> 00:16:28.066
Her father is the Lord's chosen King.

175
00:16:28.526 --> 00:16:30.659
And her father's blood
runs through her veins.

176
00:16:40.647 --> 00:16:42.294
You march on Winterfell soon.

177
00:16:42.793 --> 00:16:43.641
We must.

178
00:16:44.707 --> 00:16:46.017
To beat the snows.

179
00:16:47.414 --> 00:16:51.169
Once before you put your faith in Ser Davos
and left me behind.

180
00:16:54.396 --> 00:16:56.342
I hope you won't make that mistake again.

181
00:16:56.579 --> 00:16:57.365
I won't.

182
00:17:00.858 --> 00:17:02.105
I need you.

183
00:17:02.454 --> 00:17:04.413
You only need faith. my King.

184
00:17:09.514 --> 00:17:11.223
And you. my Lady. what do you need?

185
00:17:13.243 --> 00:17:14.678
To serve my Lord.

186
00:17:19.813 --> 00:17:20.935
Lord Ashford.

187
00:17:27.389 --> 00:17:28.724
Lenny Coalfield.

188
00:17:31.855 --> 00:17:33.339
Lord Smallwood.

189
00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.572
Never even heard of these people.

190
00:17:35.692 --> 00:17:37.460
They haven't heard of you either.

191
00:17:38.283 --> 00:17:40.454
But we need men and they have some.

192
00:17:43.069 --> 00:17:45.925
How many men does this Lord ***
have to send us?

193
00:17:46.249 --> 00:17:48.008
More than Lord Weebly.

194
00:18:01.619 --> 00:18:03.203
- Not him.
- Then who?

195
00:18:03.617 --> 00:18:06.272
I'm sorry. but we need men and supplies.

196
00:18:06.392 --> 00:18:07.954
And Roose Bolton is the Warden of...

197
00:18:08.074 --> 00:18:11.754
- He murdered my brother.
- We swore to be the Watchers on the Wall.

198
00:18:12.556 --> 00:18:15.406
We can't watch the Wall with 50 men.

199
00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:20.425
And we can't get more men without help
from the Warden of the North.

200
00:18:43.343 --> 00:18:45.000
Apologies. my Lady.

201
00:18:57.329 --> 00:18:58.791
Lord Commander.

202
00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.821
How can I help you?

203
00:19:01.674 --> 00:19:03.671
Come with us when we ride south.

204
00:19:03.791 --> 00:19:06.473
None of us know the
castle as well as you do.

205
00:19:07.131 --> 00:19:10.566
Its hidden tunnels. its weaknesses.
its people.

206
00:19:12.174 --> 00:19:14.270
Winterfell was your home once.

207
00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:18.363
Don't you want to chase the rats out of it?

208
00:19:20.867 --> 00:19:23.035
Castle Black is my home now.

209
00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:27.055
Night's Watch takes no part in
the wars of the Seven Kingdoms.

210
00:19:27.175 --> 00:19:28.712
There's only one war.

211
00:19:29.418 --> 00:19:31.392
Life against death.

212
00:19:33.219 --> 00:19:34.120
Come.

213
00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:36.466
Let me show what you're fighting for.

214
00:19:36.586 --> 00:19:38.836
You're gonna show me
some vision in the fire.

215
00:19:39.298 --> 00:19:41.007
Forgive me. my Lady.

216
00:19:41.231 --> 00:19:42.666
But I don't trust in visions.

217
00:19:44.168 --> 00:19:45.291
No visions.

218
00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.037
No magic.

219
00:19:48.035 --> 00:19:49.282
Just life.

220
00:20:09.682 --> 00:20:11.478
Do you feel my heart beating?

221
00:20:14.525 --> 00:20:20.264
This power in you. you resist it. and
that's your mistake. Embrace it.

222
00:20:31.269 --> 00:20:34.077
The Lord of Light made us male and female.

223
00:20:35.076 --> 00:20:37.598
Two parts of a greater whole.

224
00:20:38.455 --> 00:20:41.358
You're not joining this power.

225
00:20:42.309 --> 00:20:44.498
Power to make life.

226
00:20:44.618 --> 00:20:47.163
power to make light.

227
00:20:47.829 --> 00:20:50.399
and power to cast shadows.

228
00:20:50.519 --> 00:20:53.873
I don't think Stannis would
like that very much.

229
00:20:53.993 --> 00:20:56.347
Then we shouldn't tell him.

230
00:20:57.061 --> 00:20:58.859
I can't.

231
00:20:58.979 --> 00:21:00.554
Why?

232
00:21:01.325 --> 00:21:02.560
I swore a vow.

233
00:21:05.041 --> 00:21:06.873
I loved another.

234
00:21:07.555 --> 00:21:09.660
The dead don't need lovers.

235
00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:12.200
Only the living.

236
00:21:16.576 --> 00:21:17.461
I know.

237
00:21:19.632 --> 00:21:20.780
But I still love her.

238
00:21:36.261 --> 00:21:38.057
You know nothing. Jon Snow.

239
00:22:15.860 --> 00:22:17.007
Are you lonely?

240
00:22:19.207 --> 00:22:20.017
Just bored.

241
00:22:20.137 --> 00:22:23.572
My father used to tell me that boredom
indicates a lack of inner resources.

242
00:22:24.022 --> 00:22:25.331
Were you bored a lot. too?

243
00:22:26.616 --> 00:22:29.097
I know Castle Black is
no place for a child.

244
00:22:29.217 --> 00:22:30.033
I like it.

245
00:22:30.556 --> 00:22:32.016
I thought I'd be left at home.

246
00:22:33.114 --> 00:22:34.897
I know mother didn't want to bring me.

247
00:22:35.983 --> 00:22:37.080
Why do you say that?

248
00:22:39.218 --> 00:22:41.089
She told me "I don't want to bring you."

249
00:22:43.459 --> 00:22:44.619
She shouldn't have said that.

250
00:22:54.995 --> 00:22:56.654
Are you ashamed of me. father?

251
00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:09.672
When you were an infant.

252
00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:13.313
the Dornish trailer landed on Dragonstone.

253
00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:17.828
His goods were junk
except for one wooden doll.

254
00:23:19.394 --> 00:23:22.123
He'd even sewn a dress on it
in the colors of our House.

255
00:23:24.712 --> 00:23:26.309
No doubt he'd heard of your birth.

256
00:23:27.109 --> 00:23:29.978
And assumed new fathers were easy targets.

257
00:23:33.732 --> 00:23:36.963
I still remember how you smiled when
I put that doll in your cradle.

258
00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:40.608
You pressed it to your cheek.

259
00:23:47.613 --> 00:23:50.659
By the time we burnt the doll.
it was too late.

260
00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.799
I was told you would die.

261
00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:57.100
Or worse.

262
00:23:58.499 --> 00:24:00.473
The grayscale would go slow.

263
00:24:01.058 --> 00:24:04.975
Let you grow just enough to know the world
before taking it away from you.

264
00:24:05.629 --> 00:24:08.391
Everyone advised me to send
you to the ruins of Valyria

265
00:24:08.511 --> 00:24:10.512
to live out your short
life with the Stone men.

266
00:24:10.743 --> 00:24:12.714
before the sickness spread to the castle.

267
00:24:14.985 --> 00:24:16.886
I told them all to go to hell.

268
00:24:19.052 --> 00:24:21.708
I called in every maester
on this side of the world.

269
00:24:21.828 --> 00:24:24.729
Every healer. every apothecary.

270
00:24:27.068 --> 00:24:29.504
They stopped the disease
and saved your life.

271
00:24:30.674 --> 00:24:34.304
Because you did not belong across the world
with the bloody Stone men.

272
00:24:35.303 --> 00:24:38.275
You are the Princess Shireen
of House Baratheon.

273
00:24:40.529 --> 00:24:42.186
And you are my daughter.

274
00:25:44.100 --> 00:25:46.171
I thought I might find you here.

275
00:25:49.046 --> 00:25:50.800
Your Aunt Lyanna.

276
00:25:51.653 --> 00:25:53.699
My father never talked about her.

277
00:25:55.185 --> 00:25:58.085
Sometimes I'd find him down here.
lighting the candles.

278
00:25:59.888 --> 00:26:01.325
They say she was beautiful.

279
00:26:02.175 --> 00:26:03.515
I saw her once.

280
00:26:03.857 --> 00:26:06.390
I was a boy. living with
your mother's family.

281
00:26:07.170 --> 00:26:09.533
Lord Whent had a great
tourney at Harrenhal.

282
00:26:10.922 --> 00:26:12.530
Everyone was there.

283
00:26:13.017 --> 00:26:14.211
The Mad King.

284
00:26:14.577 --> 00:26:15.746
your father.

285
00:26:16.063 --> 00:26:17.549
Robert Baratheon.

286
00:26:18.743 --> 00:26:21.935
and Lyanna. She was already
promised to Robert.

287
00:26:22.716 --> 00:26:25.615
You can imagine what it was like
for me. a boy from nowhere.

288
00:26:26.005 --> 00:26:27.467
with nothing to his name.

289
00:26:28.028 --> 00:26:31.901
watching these legendary
men. tilting at the lists.

290
00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:34.494
The last two riders were

291
00:26:34.614 --> 00:26:37.457
Barristan Selmy and Rhaegar Targaryen.

292
00:26:37.846 --> 00:26:40.692
When Rhaegar won. everyone
cheered for the prince.

293
00:26:41.589 --> 00:26:45.169
I remember the girls laughing when he took off
his helmet and they saw that silver hair.

294
00:26:45.662 --> 00:26:47.458
How handsome he was.

295
00:26:47.935 --> 00:26:52.261
Until he rode right past
his wife. Elia Martell.

296
00:26:52.381 --> 00:26:54.544
and all the smiles died.

297
00:26:55.888 --> 00:26:58.569
I've never seen so many people so quiet.

298
00:26:59.452 --> 00:27:01.431
He rode past his wife

299
00:27:03.223 --> 00:27:05.942
and he lay a crown of winter
roses in Lyanna's lap.

300
00:27:06.740 --> 00:27:08.312
Blue was frost.

301
00:27:12.499 --> 00:27:16.054
How many tens of thousands had to die
because Rhaegar chose your aunt?

302
00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:20.607
Yes. he chose her.

303
00:27:21.990 --> 00:27:23.942
And then he kidnapped her and raped her.

304
00:27:32.506 --> 00:27:33.454
Come.

305
00:27:34.564 --> 00:27:36.884
Let's speak somewhere
the dead can't hear us.

306
00:27:42.329 --> 00:27:44.612
- Dressed for riding?
- I am.

307
00:27:46.682 --> 00:27:47.593
Where are you going?

308
00:27:48.304 --> 00:27:49.938
King's Landing.

309
00:27:50.400 --> 00:27:51.398
King's Landing?

310
00:27:52.037 --> 00:27:53.816
Cersei sent for me.

311
00:27:54.291 --> 00:27:56.224
We must not let her sniff out any trouble.

312
00:27:57.073 --> 00:27:58.782
You can't leave me here.

313
00:27:58.902 --> 00:28:01.775
I know how hard it is to live with
people you despise. believe me.

314
00:28:02.945 --> 00:28:04.305
But it won't be for long.

315
00:28:04.879 --> 00:28:06.051
How do you know?

316
00:28:07.615 --> 00:28:10.584
Stannis Baratheon garrisons
at Castle Black.

317
00:28:11.367 --> 00:28:15.125
He'll march south to King's Landing
before the winter snows block his way.

318
00:28:15.245 --> 00:28:17.803
But first. he has to take Winterfell.

319
00:28:18.576 --> 00:28:20.701
- You don't know that.
- I do.

320
00:28:21.857 --> 00:28:24.001
Once he liberates these
lands from the Boltons

321
00:28:24.121 --> 00:28:26.462
he'll rally your father's
bannermen to his cause.

322
00:28:26.726 --> 00:28:27.960
With the North behind him.

323
00:28:28.609 --> 00:28:30.867
Stannis can finally take the Iron Throne.

324
00:28:31.372 --> 00:28:32.906
You think he'll defeat the Boltons?

325
00:28:34.160 --> 00:28:35.756
He has a larger army.

326
00:28:35.876 --> 00:28:38.139
He's the finest military
commander in Westeros.

327
00:28:38.259 --> 00:28:41.494
A betting man would put
his money on Stannis.

328
00:28:42.185 --> 00:28:44.500
As it happens. I am a betting man.

329
00:28:45.799 --> 00:28:47.209
And if you're right?

330
00:28:47.808 --> 00:28:49.342
Stannis takes Winterfell.

331
00:28:49.917 --> 00:28:52.662
he rescues you from the most
despised family in the North.

332
00:28:53.111 --> 00:28:56.042
Grateful for your late father's
courageous support for his claim.

333
00:28:56.162 --> 00:28:58.343
he names you Wardeness of the North.

334
00:28:59.444 --> 00:29:01.986
But I... I wouldn't...

335
00:29:02.719 --> 00:29:06.305
- Wardeness of the North...
- You are the last surviving Stark.

336
00:29:07.144 --> 00:29:08.242
He needs you.

337
00:29:09.042 --> 00:29:10.102
What if you're wrong?

338
00:29:10.222 --> 00:29:14.094
What if Stannis never attacks Winterfell.
or he does and the Boltons defeat him?

339
00:29:14.759 --> 00:29:18.131
Then you will this Bolton boy. Ramsay.
and make him yours.

340
00:29:19.008 --> 00:29:21.912
- I don't know how to do that.
- Of course you do.

341
00:29:22.380 --> 00:29:24.426
He's already fallen for you.

342
00:29:24.546 --> 00:29:28.675
- His father frightens me.
- He should. he's a dangerous man.

343
00:29:29.991 --> 00:29:33.207
But even the most dangerous
men can be outmaneuvered.

344
00:29:33.707 --> 00:29:36.252
And you learned to maneuver
from the very best.

345
00:29:38.572 --> 00:29:40.418
I return before too long.

346
00:29:40.788 --> 00:29:42.509
You'll be strong without me.

347
00:29:51.481 --> 00:29:53.575
The North will be yours.

348
00:29:54.622 --> 00:29:57.429
Do you believe me?

349
00:29:59.333 --> 00:30:02.331
I expect I'll be a married woman
by the time you return.

350
00:31:05.858 --> 00:31:08.654
Breakfast.

351
00:31:11.866 --> 00:31:13.812
That would have been a shit way to die.

352
00:31:13.932 --> 00:31:16.394
As far as I've seen. they're
all shot way to die.

353
00:31:16.626 --> 00:31:20.015
Aye. But y'all ought to give
the singers a good ending.

354
00:31:20.135 --> 00:31:22.275
I don't care what's sung about me
when I'm dead.

355
00:31:22.930 --> 00:31:24.417
No?

356
00:31:25.090 --> 00:31:27.718
Two knights. off to rescue a princess.

357
00:31:28.118 --> 00:31:31.236
- Sounds like a good song to me.
- Sounds like all the rest.

358
00:31:34.726 --> 00:31:39.008
What about you? What shit
way would you choose?

359
00:31:39.901 --> 00:31:46.325
In my own keep. drinking my own wine.
watching my son gravel from a fortune.

360
00:31:46.445 --> 00:31:51.500
How disappointing. I thought you'd
have something more exciting planned.

361
00:31:52.845 --> 00:31:56.615
I've had an exciting life.
I want my death to be boring.

362
00:31:58.340 --> 00:32:02.563
- How do you want to go?
- In the arms of the woman I love.

363
00:32:06.202 --> 00:32:08.869
She want the same thing?

364
00:32:13.619 --> 00:32:14.695
Let's go.

365
00:32:25.288 --> 00:32:26.910
The captain to that ship...

366
00:32:27.424 --> 00:32:29.795
- What was he. Braavosi?
- Pentoshi.

367
00:32:30.777 --> 00:32:32.055
And he's headed to Oldtown.

368
00:32:32.277 --> 00:32:33.387
As I said.

369
00:32:33.507 --> 00:32:34.522
Why?

370
00:32:35.033 --> 00:32:37.011
What's to stop him from
docking down the coast

371
00:32:37.131 --> 00:32:39.730
and telling the locals that
Jaime Lannister's in Dorne?

372
00:32:39.850 --> 00:32:40.915
A bag of gold.

373
00:32:42.019 --> 00:32:43.625
I'm not sure you understand

374
00:32:43.745 --> 00:32:46.182
how much people hate your family
in this part of the world.

375
00:32:46.302 --> 00:32:47.897
It was a heavy bag.

376
00:32:48.194 --> 00:32:50.626
And I bet he swore all
kinds of oaths to get it.

377
00:32:51.172 --> 00:32:52.981
But you won't be around if he breaks them.

378
00:33:02.792 --> 00:33:04.149
How many you count?

379
00:33:04.269 --> 00:33:05.240
Four.

380
00:33:05.739 --> 00:33:07.330
How many you think you can take?

381
00:33:07.450 --> 00:33:09.513
One. if he's slow.

382
00:33:13.012 --> 00:33:14.353
Halt!

383
00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:20.356
Fucked in the arse.

384
00:33:25.580 --> 00:33:26.562
Hiya!

385
00:33:30.991 --> 00:33:33.158
Morning. lads.

386
00:33:33.423 --> 00:33:35.185
Glad we found you.

387
00:33:35.684 --> 00:33:36.744
Who are you?

388
00:33:37.218 --> 00:33:38.325
Cooper.

389
00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:40.211
This is Darnell.

390
00:33:40.508 --> 00:33:42.004
You're from King's Landing.

391
00:33:42.254 --> 00:33:43.782
Accent gave you away?

392
00:33:45.544 --> 00:33:46.324
Flea Bottom.

393
00:33:46.444 --> 00:33:47.836
Whelped and whipped.

394
00:33:48.148 --> 00:33:49.302
Why are you here?

395
00:33:49.422 --> 00:33:50.947
Our ship capsized in the night.

396
00:33:51.259 --> 00:33:52.647
We managed to swim ashore.

397
00:33:53.551 --> 00:33:54.690
It was a near thing. really.

398
00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:57.465
I thought the sharks would get us.

399
00:33:58.884 --> 00:34:00.599
There are no sharks in Dorne.

400
00:34:02.316 --> 00:34:04.436
I could have sworn those were shark fins.

401
00:34:05.727 --> 00:34:07.725
Dolphins maybe.

402
00:34:08.821 --> 00:34:10.600
Throw your swords in the sand.

403
00:34:11.033 --> 00:34:13.216
Boys. there's no need for this.

404
00:34:13.548 --> 00:34:16.237
Just. point us in the right direction.

405
00:34:16.357 --> 00:34:17.719
We'll find our way home.

406
00:34:17.839 --> 00:34:19.021
Swords in the sand!

407
00:34:19.313 --> 00:34:20.600
Now!

408
00:34:48.054 --> 00:34:49.311
That one should be slow enough.

409
00:35:43.289 --> 00:35:44.903
Nice move!

410
00:35:46.730 --> 00:35:48.101
Luck.

411
00:35:48.923 --> 00:35:51.298
You had a wonderful teacher.

412
00:36:04.602 --> 00:36:06.804
Always wanted a Dornish stallion.

413
00:36:07.604 --> 00:36:11.131
Beasts can run a day and
night without tiring.

414
00:36:11.465 --> 00:36:14.388
We'll ride to the Water Gardens
with a nice breeze in our face.

415
00:36:14.508 --> 00:36:16.776
But first we need to bury these bodies.

416
00:36:17.239 --> 00:36:18.701
Birds have to eat too.

417
00:36:18.821 --> 00:36:20.953
Corpses raise questions.
questions raise armies.

418
00:36:21.073 --> 00:36:22.707
We're not here to start a war.

419
00:36:23.584 --> 00:36:26.191
Do you know how long it will
take us to dig all those holes?

420
00:36:26.824 --> 00:36:29.261
I can't dig very well with one hand.

421
00:36:29.992 --> 00:36:31.429
Not at all. really.

422
00:37:02.344 --> 00:37:03.757
Nama...

423
00:37:10.068 --> 00:37:12.772
- Nym. Obara.
- Will it be war?

424
00:37:12.892 --> 00:37:16.037
Prince Doran will weep for your father.
but nothing else.

425
00:37:16.157 --> 00:37:18.595
We must avenge Oberyn ourselves.

426
00:37:18.715 --> 00:37:22.298
Without Doran we have no army to
march against the Lannisters.

427
00:37:22.675 --> 00:37:25.013
We don't need an army to start a war.

428
00:37:25.540 --> 00:37:28.814
Queen Cersei loves her children.

429
00:37:28.934 --> 00:37:32.050
- ...and we have one of them.
- We may have a problem.

430
00:37:38.151 --> 00:37:43.024
A ship's captain. who found me in Planky
Town. claiming he had information to sell.

431
00:37:43.144 --> 00:37:46.374
He told me he smuggled Jaime
Lannister into Dorne.

432
00:37:48.277 --> 00:37:49.512
He's come for Myrcella.

433
00:37:51.066 --> 00:37:52.862
If he gets to her before we do.

434
00:37:52.982 --> 00:37:55.132
we lose our only chance for revenge.

435
00:37:56.168 --> 00:37:57.428
You must choose...

436
00:37:58.775 --> 00:38:00.646
Doran's way and peace.

437
00:38:00.972 --> 00:38:02.257
or my way...

438
00:38:02.831 --> 00:38:04.128
and war.

439
00:38:06.473 --> 00:38:08.407
I'm with you. Always.

440
00:38:09.492 --> 00:38:10.303
Nym?

441
00:38:15.349 --> 00:38:16.409
Obara?

442
00:38:18.093 --> 00:38:20.937
When I was a child. Oberyn
came to take me to court.

443
00:38:21.989 --> 00:38:23.923
I'd never seen this man. and yet

444
00:38:24.043 --> 00:38:25.769
he called himself my father.

445
00:38:26.393 --> 00:38:30.272
My mother wept. said
I was too young. and a girl.

446
00:38:33.312 --> 00:38:36.131
Oberyn tossed his spear
at my feet and said

447
00:38:36.380 --> 00:38:38.339
"Girl or boy. we
fight our battles.

448
00:38:39.312 --> 00:38:41.532
"But the Gods let us
choose our weapons."

449
00:38:42.568 --> 00:38:44.603
My father pointed to the spear.

450
00:38:45.092 --> 00:38:47.468
and then to my mother's tears.

451
00:38:54.632 --> 00:38:56.388
I made my choice long ago.

452
00:39:30.920 --> 00:39:31.858
Thank you.

453
00:39:40.866 --> 00:39:41.734
Who are you?

454
00:39:42.516 --> 00:39:43.574
Your captor.

455
00:39:46.372 --> 00:39:47.510
Do you have wine?

456
00:39:47.730 --> 00:39:48.867
No.

457
00:39:50.125 --> 00:39:51.592
I can't sleep without wine.

458
00:39:51.712 --> 00:39:53.039
Then stay awake.

459
00:39:59.666 --> 00:40:01.083
You're going the wrong way.

460
00:40:02.666 --> 00:40:04.691
My sister's in Westeros.

461
00:40:05.130 --> 00:40:07.206
Westeros...is west!

462
00:40:07.705 --> 00:40:08.643
We're heading east...

463
00:40:09.689 --> 00:40:11.714
I'm not taking you
to your sister.

464
00:40:13.301 --> 00:40:15.506
You said you were
taking me to the Queen.

465
00:40:15.626 --> 00:40:16.385
I am.

466
00:40:16.854 --> 00:40:18.760
Queen Daenerys Targaryen.

467
00:40:19.094 --> 00:40:20.581
She's the Queen I serve.

468
00:40:27.463 --> 00:40:29.279
What a waste of a
good kidnapping.

469
00:40:30.916 --> 00:40:32.832
So happens I was
heading there myself!

470
00:40:33.271 --> 00:40:35.247
What business would you
have with the Queen?

471
00:40:35.367 --> 00:40:36.785
Gold and glory?

472
00:40:37.055 --> 00:40:38.192
Oh. and hate.

473
00:40:39.190 --> 00:40:41.286
If you've ever met my
sister. you'd understand.

474
00:40:42.723 --> 00:40:43.421
So...

475
00:40:43.541 --> 00:40:46.069
now that it's clear
we're on the same side.

476
00:40:56.292 --> 00:40:59.216
A high born knight from
the North of Westeros.

477
00:40:59.336 --> 00:41:01.062
down on his luck in Essos.

478
00:41:02.228 --> 00:41:03.216
Dragon epaulettes?

479
00:41:03.855 --> 00:41:05.781
Bear sigil breast plate.

480
00:41:07.058 --> 00:41:08.695
You're Jorah Mormont.

481
00:41:10.522 --> 00:41:11.929
I have to ask...

482
00:41:12.169 --> 00:41:15.173
how. exactly. were you
serving your Queen in a whore house.

483
00:41:15.293 --> 00:41:16.540
half a world away?

484
00:41:17.376 --> 00:41:18.593
Is it possible.

485
00:41:18.713 --> 00:41:20.090
that you were running?

486
00:41:20.948 --> 00:41:22.026
Why would you be running?

487
00:41:22.844 --> 00:41:24.721
And why would she
have sent you away?

488
00:41:25.360 --> 00:41:27.060
Oh. wait!

489
00:41:27.878 --> 00:41:30.497
You were spying on
her. weren't you?

490
00:41:31.402 --> 00:41:32.634
It's all coming back to me!

491
00:41:33.008 --> 00:41:36.750
I was drunk through most of the Small
Council meetings. but it's all coming back.

492
00:41:37.046 --> 00:41:39.962
You passed notes to
Varys's little birds.

493
00:41:41.740 --> 00:41:43.804
She found out. didn't she?

494
00:41:44.225 --> 00:41:46.424
Found out. and exiled you.

495
00:41:47.968 --> 00:41:50.900
And now you hope to win
back her favor with a gift.

496
00:41:52.814 --> 00:41:54.349
A risky scheme...

497
00:41:54.948 --> 00:41:57.255
One might even say. desperate.

498
00:41:59.062 --> 00:42:02.430
Do you think Daenerys would
execute me. and pardon you?

499
00:42:03.713 --> 00:42:06.192
I'd say the reverse
is just as likely.

500
00:42:27.846 --> 00:42:29.991
Everyone looks happy
enough from up here.

501
00:42:31.400 --> 00:42:32.911
What?

502
00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:35.929
I was thinking of all the
times your brother

503
00:42:36.260 --> 00:42:39.880
made me go with him down from the Red
Keep. into the streets of King's Landing.

504
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:42.462
- Why?
- He liked to walk among the people.

505
00:42:42.582 --> 00:42:44.064
he liked to sing to them.

506
00:42:45.228 --> 00:42:46.463
He sang to them?

507
00:42:46.583 --> 00:42:47.866
Yes.

508
00:42:48.352 --> 00:42:50.685
Rhaegar would take a
spot on the Hook

509
00:42:50.990 --> 00:42:53.522
or the Street of Seeds
and he'd sing.

510
00:42:54.108 --> 00:42:55.518
Just like all the
other minstrels.

511
00:42:55.638 --> 00:42:56.846
And what did you do?

512
00:42:56.966 --> 00:42:58.692
I made sure no one killed him.

513
00:42:59.042 --> 00:43:00.813
And... I collected the money.

514
00:43:02.525 --> 00:43:03.889
Well... he liked to see
how much he could make.

515
00:43:04.009 --> 00:43:05.936
- He was good?
- He was very good.

516
00:43:06.056 --> 00:43:06.984
Viserys never told you?

517
00:43:07.343 --> 00:43:09.975
He told me Rhaegar was
good at killing people.

518
00:43:10.986 --> 00:43:12.295
Rhaegar never liked killing.

519
00:43:12.709 --> 00:43:13.956
He loved singing.

520
00:43:14.455 --> 00:43:15.839
And what did you
do with the money?

521
00:43:15.959 --> 00:43:18.983
Well. one time. we gave it to the
next minstrel down the street.

522
00:43:19.320 --> 00:43:21.827
One time. he gave it to an
orphanage in Flea Bottom.

523
00:43:21.947 --> 00:43:23.037
One time...

524
00:43:24.108 --> 00:43:25.493
we got horribly drunk.

525
00:43:27.401 --> 00:43:28.586
Your Grace.

526
00:43:29.771 --> 00:43:32.428
Hizdahr is here. waiting
in the audience chamber.

527
00:43:33.960 --> 00:43:35.395
How many others are there?

528
00:43:35.515 --> 00:43:37.715
Fifty... a hundred.

529
00:43:37.835 --> 00:43:40.110
Will you be joining
us. Ser Barristan?

530
00:43:40.230 --> 00:43:43.637
I think I can protect
you from Hizdhar Zo Loraq.

531
00:43:43.757 --> 00:43:46.079
I think I can protect me
from Hizdhar Zo Loraq.

532
00:43:47.601 --> 00:43:49.223
Go. Ser Barristan.

533
00:43:49.343 --> 00:43:50.732
Sing a song for me.

534
00:43:51.244 --> 00:43:52.454
Your Grace.

535
00:43:57.832 --> 00:43:59.354
All men must die.

536
00:43:59.628 --> 00:44:01.973
- But not all can die in glory.
- Glory?

537
00:44:02.235 --> 00:44:03.545
Why else do men fight?

538
00:44:03.767 --> 00:44:07.334
Why did your ancestors cross the Narrow
Sea and conquer the Seven Kingdoms?

539
00:44:07.454 --> 00:44:09.483
So their names would live on.

540
00:44:09.944 --> 00:44:12.751
Those who find victory in the fighting
pits. will never become kings...

541
00:44:12.871 --> 00:44:14.727
but their names will live on.

542
00:44:15.089 --> 00:44:16.898
It's the best chance
they'll ever have.

543
00:44:17.018 --> 00:44:21.382
Is that what you used to tell men before you
set them to butchering each other for sport?

544
00:44:21.502 --> 00:44:24.202
Your Grace. today is the traditional
start of the fighting season.

545
00:44:24.322 --> 00:44:26.083
I do not recognize this tradition.

546
00:44:26.203 --> 00:44:28.016
Traditions are the only thing

547
00:44:28.136 --> 00:44:30.764
that will hold this city...
your city. together.

548
00:44:33.005 --> 00:44:36.310
Without them. former slaves and former
masters have nothing in common.

549
00:44:38.344 --> 00:44:40.502
Nothing but centuries of mistrust

550
00:44:40.622 --> 00:44:41.599
and resentment.

551
00:44:42.806 --> 00:44:45.326
I can't promise this is the
answer to all our problems...

552
00:44:46.684 --> 00:44:47.969
but it's a start.

553
00:45:25.034 --> 00:45:26.651
_

554
00:48:57.845 --> 00:49:07.976
